course: dictionary
lesson: 10164
title: Ti: one short word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ti is a very short word, so you cannot tell what it means from the letters alone. Look at the words around it. If the sentence is about singing, ti is a note. If it is about plants or chemistry, it means something else. Always ask: what is this sentence about?
explain: «Picture a class clapping "ta, ta, ti-ti, ta".» Here ti is a sound in a rhythm, not a note name. Ti-ti is two quick sounds that share one beat, and ta is one full beat. Saying a rhythm out loud before you play it helps your body feel the long and short sounds.
explain: «Ghoti» is a joke spelling of fish, with ti sounding like the sh in «nation». The clue is that it is a joke: real English does not use those letters that way at the start or end of a word, so you should not copy it as a rule.
fact: Ti (also spelled te) is the seventh note in the singing scale: do, re, mi, fa, so, la, ti, do.
fact: Ti is just below the top do, so it leads you back up to the top do.
fact: Ti is also the name of the cabbage tree, a plant in New Zealand and the Pacific.
fact: As a fragment, «ti» often comes from a longer word cut in the middle, or from Ti, the chemistry symbol for titanium.
fact: In the Kodaly method, «ta» is one beat and «ti-ti» is two half-beat sounds.
exercise: In a singing lesson the teacher sings «do re mi fa so la ti do». What is ti here? | A joke spelling of fish | *A note in the singing scale | A kind of bird | A plant in New Zealand
exercise: In Tano, «Ti ama» means "I like" and «Ti ne ama» means "I don't like". What does ne mean in «Ti ne ama»? | Like | Very | Yesterday | *Not
exercise: «The ti grew tall on the hillside in New Zealand.» What is ti here? | A symbol for titanium | *A plant, the cabbage tree | A rhythm sound in a clap | A note in the singing scale
test: In «Ghoti», the ti is pronounced like which sound in «nation»? | ee | oh | t | *sh
test: In the clapping rhythm «ta, ta, ti-ti, ta», how many beats does «ti-ti» share? | Half a beat each, so none at all | Four | *One beat, shared by two quick sounds | Two beats, one each
exam: Ti is the chemistry symbol for which metal? | *Titanium | Tin | Zinc | Iron
